  "vikisozluk_etimolojiler": [
    {
      "metin": "Disputed etymology with most connecting it back to عُمَانَة (ʕumāna) considered a by-name of the city صُحَار (ṣuḥār), the most prevalent city-state at the time the name became associated with the region as a whole. Considered derived from the root ع م ن (ʕ m n) meaning, \"to settle or remain\", \"to dwell\", \"a place where one enters and chooses to stay\", \"to be abiding or a lasting settlement\", \"a plain or easy country\".",
